meta {
  name: Exchange OAuth callback
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/connect/exchange/callback?code=REPLACE&state=REPLACE
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # GET /api/connect/exchange/callback

  Where Coinbase/Bybit send the browser after a read-only grant. This is a
  browser round-trip, not a normal API call: it reads the signed state cookie
  (`tl_oauth_state`) and the session, exchanges the code, verifies the
  credential with a real read-only call, and stores the connection sealed.

  You cannot meaningfully drive this from Bruno by hand: `code` and `state` come
  from the exchange and the state must match the httpOnly cookie set when the
  flow started. It is here for completeness. It always redirects to
  `/dashboard/settings?saved=...` or `?error=...`.

  To exercise it: start the flow in the app (Settings -> Connect exchange), then
  copy the `code` and `state` query params from the exchange redirect here and
  replay it in the same browser profile that holds the cookie.
}
